t2_cuda_n7000 replicate 5: wall 2.29 s against 1.00-1.03 s for the other ten.
Its step phase is normal (RESULT_T_PER_STEP 0.00146 s, RESULT_T_TOTAL 0.31 s,
the same kernels and kernel time as replicate 4), so the extra 1.3 s was spent
outside the simulation: process start, CUDA context creation or model
construction. Nothing in the log marks it. Kept, as every accepted run is; it
widens the end-to-end error bar at N = 7000 on the A40 in fig_trees (the step
panel is unaffected). Noted 2026-10-09 when the figures were drawn.
